{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790257749,"nonce":"mvOfX9iVqwTLi1OkDMT2B1rdPWU=","title":"Lua typer: debug.setmetatable attaches a metatable the types do not follow","message":"`debug.setmetatable(t, mt)` is typed as an ordinary library call: `t`'s shape escapes but gets neither the class nor `unknown_meta`, so a read of a field the shape lacks is typed nil and `__index` is never consulted by typed code. `metatable_builtin` in crates/zyntax_lua/src/types.rs handles only the base `setmetatable`.\n\nReproducer (lua5.4 prints `found y?`, zylua at dea6d08b prints `nil`):\n\n    local t = { x = 1 }\n    debug.setmetatable(t, { __index = function(_, k) return k .. \"?\" end })\n    local v = t.y\n    if v then print(\"found\", v) else print(\"nil\") end\n\nFix: treat `debug.setmetatable` as `setmetatable` for shapes (class when the metatable is a known shape, else `unknown_meta`), and as `blind_setmetatable` for receivers the types do not know. Found while closing the blind-read escape holes (package l3-escape-holes); not fixed there.","files":null}]}